1. Consumer receives message
2. Consumer processes message (e.g. sends email)
3. Consumer sends ACK to broker

// If the process crashes at step 2.5 (after email, before ACK):
4. Broker re-delivers message
5. Consumer sends email AGAIN

// Solution: store a processed message ID before sending
if (processedIds.contains(message.id)) return; // already done
sendEmail(message);
processedIds.add(message.id);
sendAck();

